Privacy Policy — ProCare Family
Effective Date: September 16, 2024 Last Updated: September 17, 2026

ProCare Family ("ProCare", "we", "our", or "us") is a healthcare care-coordination application developed and managed by BigFatAILabs. ProCare Family helps family members stay informed about and participate in the home nursing care of their loved ones.

The application provides features including care dashboards, care plans, medication tracking, vital history, AI-assisted care coordination, reports, billing and payments, family access, caregiver feedback, and notifications.

We are committed to protecting personal information and sensitive healthcare information handled through ProCare.

By downloading, accessing, or using ProCare Family, you acknowledge the practices described in this Privacy Policy.

1. Information We Collect
Depending on how you use ProCare Family, we may collect the following categories of information.

1.1 Account and Profile Information
When you create or use a ProCare Family account, we may collect:

Full name
Mobile phone number
Email address
Profile photograph, if provided
Login and authentication information
Family relationship or role
Account preferences
Information relating to your access permissions
This information is used to create and manage your account, authenticate you, provide appropriate access to care information, and communicate with you about the service.

1.2 Patient and Care Information
ProCare Family may provide access to information relating to a family member or patient receiving home nursing care.

This may include:

Patient name and profile information
Health and care information
Blood pressure
Heart rate
SpO₂
Temperature
Other recorded vital measurements
Medication schedules and medication-related records
Care tasks and task completion status
Nurse check-in information
Nurse notes and care notes
Care activities and timelines
Care plans
Relevant medical or care history
Care-related alerts and observations
This information is used to help authorized family members monitor and coordinate home nursing care.

Health and patient information is treated as sensitive information and is only made available to users who have appropriate authorization or access permissions.

1.3 Caregiver and Nursing Information
ProCare Family may display information about caregivers or nurses involved in a patient's care, including:

Caregiver or nurse name
Profile photograph, where available
Assigned role
Check-in status
Care activity information
Shift or visit information
Care notes associated with the patient's care
Caregiver ratings or appreciation submitted through the application
This information is displayed to authorized users for care coordination and transparency.

1.4 Care Plan and Medication Information
The application may collect and display information relating to:

Daily care tasks
Task completion
Medication schedules
Medication administration records
Care instructions
Nurse notes
Upcoming and completed activities
Care-plan progress
This information allows family members to understand the current status of their loved one's care.

1.5 Vitals and Health History
ProCare may collect and display health measurements recorded as part of the patient's care, including:

SpO₂
Blood pressure
Heart rate
Temperature
Other care-related vital measurements
Historical readings may be retained so that authorized users can review trends and generate care reports.

1.6 AI Care Coordinator
ProCare Family provides an AI-assisted care coordination feature that may allow users to:

Ask care-related questions
Request information about care activities
Request supplies or care-related actions
Interact through text
Send voice messages
Upload files where supported
Information submitted to the AI Care Coordinator may include messages, care-related information, uploaded files, and other information necessary to respond to the user's request.

AI-generated responses are intended to assist with care coordination and general information. They should not be considered a replacement for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or emergency medical services.

Important: If ProCare uses an external AI provider to process these conversations, that provider should be explicitly named in this section and in your Google Play Data Safety disclosures.

1.7 Reports and Documents
ProCare may allow users to generate and access weekly, monthly, or other care-related reports.

Reports may contain:

Patient information
Vital readings
Medication information
Care-plan progress
Nurse or caregiver notes
Care activity information
Other information associated with the patient's care
Users may also choose to share reports with trusted individuals or healthcare professionals through available sharing features.

Where the application provides expiring links or other access controls, these mechanisms are intended to limit access to shared information.

1.8 Files, Photos, and Camera
ProCare may request access to your device's camera or files when required for features such as:

Uploading care-related documents
Uploading supporting files
Capturing profile photographs
Uploading information requested through the AI Care Coordinator
Sharing care-related documentation
Access to your camera, photos, or files is requested only when required for the relevant feature.

You may revoke these permissions through your device settings. Revoking access may prevent certain features from functioning.

1.9 Voice Messages
If you use voice messaging or voice-related functionality, ProCare may process:

Voice recordings
Audio files
Transcribed content, where applicable
Voice information is used to provide the requested communication or care-coordination functionality.

If voice recordings are processed by a third-party transcription or AI provider, the relevant provider should be identified in the Third-Party Services section.

1.10 Family Access Information
ProCare allows users to invite family members and assign different access roles.

Depending on the role assigned, invited family members may be able to access some or all relevant care information.

The available roles may include:

Admin
Member
View
The information accessible to each user is determined by the permissions configured for the account and patient.

Users are responsible for only inviting people they trust and assigning appropriate access permissions.

1.11 Billing and Payment Information
ProCare may provide billing and payment functionality, including:

Invoices
Payment status
Payment history
Payment requests
Billing disputes
Payment-extension requests
Payments may be processed through Razorpay or other payment service providers.

ProCare does not need to directly store your complete card or banking credentials when payment processing is handled by the applicable payment provider.

Payment providers may collect and process payment information according to their own privacy policies and terms.

1.12 Notifications
ProCare uses push notifications to provide timely updates relating to the service.

Notifications may include:

Medication reminders
Nurse check-in updates
Care-plan updates
Vital-related alerts
Care activity updates
Invoice and payment notifications
Family access updates
Care coordination messages
Push notifications may be delivered using Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM).

You can disable notifications through your device settings, although doing so may prevent you from receiving important care-related updates.

1.13 Device and Technical Information
When you use ProCare, we may automatically receive certain technical information necessary to operate and maintain the application, such as:

Device type and model
Operating system and version
Application version
Network information
IP address
Crash information
Diagnostic information
Performance information
Device identifiers where technically required by the application or service providers
This information is used for application security, troubleshooting, performance monitoring, and service improvement.

1.14 Biometric Authentication
Where supported by your device, ProCare may allow biometric authentication such as fingerprint or facial authentication.

Biometric information used by the device's authentication system is generally processed by the operating system rather than being directly collected or stored by ProCare.

ProCare uses the authentication result provided by the device to help secure access to the application.

